      "problem": "What number can be added to $-40$ to get a sum of $0?$",
      "worked_solution": "The number that can be added to $-40$ to give $0$ is the additive inverse of $-40.$\n\nTo find the additive inverse of the number $-40$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain\n\n$$\n-\\,(-40)=40.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n(-40)+40=-40+40=0\\,✓\n$$",
